    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0327" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-11T12:00:00+09:00">September 11,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 11—5:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>361. Department’s 194, September 8, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d349-f1"/>
                    access by businessmen to Northern District Shanghai.</p>
                <pb facs="0328" n="320" xml:id="pg320"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>A member of my staff took up the matter with Yoshizawa<anchor n="21"
                            xml:id="d349-f2"/> at the Foreign Office yesterday morning, leaving an
                            <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>My British colleague proposes to act along the same lines. My French
                        colleague will act if he hears from his colleague at Nanking. My German
                        colleague has already made an oral approach on the basis of instructions
                        from Berlin previous to the receipt of my letter to him. My Italian
                        colleague made an oral approach yesterday.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for relay to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d349-f1" n="20" xml:id="d349-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it repeated Shanghai’s No. 667, September 7, 8 p.m., <ref
                        target="#pg313">p. 313</ref>, and instructed the Ambassador that after
                    consultation with his interested colleagues he might, in his discretion, make an
                    informal approach to the Japanese Government (393.115/55).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d349-f2" n="21" xml:id="d349-f2-content">
                <p>Seijiro Yoshizawa, Director of the American Affairs Bureau, Japanese Foreign
                    Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
